    "created_at": "2016-08-17T17:04:04Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-08-17T17:04:04Z",
    "body": "Yeah, that's easy - if you invoke the [\"parse according to a CSS grammar\"](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-syntax/#parse-grammar) hook, you'll get back abstract CSS values you can work on (or it'll return failure).  You can then just branch on whether it matched the `none` branch, and that's unambiguous. \n",
